      "formation_structure": {
        "artillery_allocation": "Steward owns the lower eastern passes; Durin contributes around upper infantry contention. GALLUS contributes on the western approach, and Lava owns the final western passage and wait. Midnight receives no anti-air damage credit.",
        "capacity": "Maximum eight simultaneous rarity-2/3 operators. Midnight leaves before Lava enters; Durin leaves before Beagle enters. Inspected current runtime exempts rarity-1 operators from this counter.",
        "economy": {
          "basis": "Initial 10 DP, natural 1 DP/s, Fang grants at 570/1320/2070/2820 and Vanilla grants at 750/1650/2550.",
          "excluded_income": "No kill DP, unsupported talent income, death refunds or later vanguard income.",
          "interpretation": "Missing income or refund indicates a survival or handoff failure; it does not authorize an alternative arithmetic ledger.",
          "living_refunds": "Vanilla 5, Lancet 1, Fang 5, Midnight 8, Durin 6, Friston 1 and Castle 1, each dependent on a successful living retreat.",
          "static_result": "Read-only conditional ledger remains nonnegative, with 0 DP immediately after Midnight's deployment at 2400. No redeployment is scheduled."
        },
        "medical_contention": "Eastern medic self-treatment competes with interceptor treatment. Plume and Melantha use supported attack skills during the route-17/16 pairs to reduce that competing damage. Ansel's second skill extends west before Lava's artillery exposure.",
        "medical_geometry": "Hibiscus [5,7] LEFT covers Cardigan [4,5], Steward [5,5], Melantha [6,5] and herself. Ansel [2,7] LEFT covers Plume [1,5], Durin [2,5], the forward upper blocker [3,5], Beagle [3,4] and himself. Each eastern medic is two columns from the corresponding caster, outside a medic-centered 1.2-radius splash.",
        "opening": "Fang, Vanilla, Plume and Melantha retain their demonstrated opening tiles and facings. Lancet retains effective central coverage.",
        "western_geometry": "GALLUS [2,3] RIGHT covers the forward upper blocker [3,5]. Lava [2,2] RIGHT covers Beagle [3,4] and roadblock #1. Beagle-centered splash misses both western casters diagonally. Lava-centered splash can kill adjacent GALLUS; his survival through that window and any death refund are not credited."
      },
